      "title": "Mother flagged faulty smoke alarms before house fire that killed father and five children, court hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/russell-island-house-fire-inquest-father-five-children-killed-faulty-smoke-alarms",
      "description": "<p>Pre-inquest conference into Queensland deaths hears witnesses did not hear any smoke alarms during 2023 fire</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A landlord was repeatedly warned about improperly installed smoke alarms before a house fire that killed a father and five children in Queensland in 2023, a coroner has heard.</p><p>Deputy state coroner Donald MacKenzie held a pre-inquest conference into the Russell Island deaths on Tuesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/russell-island-house-fire-inquest-father-five-children-killed-faulty-smoke-alarms\">Continue reading...</a>",
